    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0529" n="1039" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1039"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/5–2448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Burdett</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">
                            niact
                        </hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-24T12:00:00+04:00">May 24,
                            1948—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>725. Deptel 457 May 23.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d313-f1"/> In view of friendly relations informally maintained with
                    Transjordan officials by this ConGen would Dept wish consider suggestion that we
                    transmit to King Abdullah or Transjordan Prime Minister personal message from
                        Stabler<anchor n="2" xml:id="d313-f2"/> or alternatively from “American
                    Consulate General” along following lines:</p>
                <p>US Government gravely disturbed by present-course developments in Palestine and
                    hopes that Transjordan Government will find it possible to cooperate in the
                    carrying out of the cease-fire which is proposed for all fronts in Palestine to
                    come into effect at 1800 hours local Arab time tonight. Embassy (or we) shall be
                    glad to transmit to the Department of State any reply which Your Majesty (or the
                    Transjordan Government) may desire to send.</p>
                <p>Department’s urgent instructions requested as we understand Arab League Political
                    Committee is now meeting in Amman.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d313-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Burdett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d313-f1" n="1" xml:id="d313-f1-content">
                <p>This was a repeat of No. 641 to Cairo, <ref target="#pg1033">p. 1033</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d313-f2" n="2" xml:id="d313-f2-content">
                <p>Wells Stabler, Vice Consul at Jerusalem.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d313-f3" n="3" xml:id="d313-f3-content">
                <p>The Department, on May 24, approved the suggestion for an informal approach by
                    the Consulate General to the Transjordan Government regarding a cease-fire
                    (telegram 458 to Jerusalem, 501.BB Palestine/5–2448).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
